      "writtenOn": "2018-09-12T10:03:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The following is the result we measured:\n(Environment: CPU clock is 48Mhz and pull the __mulsf3 routine into the section of ram code)\n-  This patch: 3 ~ 4 us.\n-  Software floating-point multiply of GCC: 4 ~ 5 us.\n(https://github.com/gcc-mirror/gcc/blob/26f8bcbd5ca246308c1dfc17e71d01ccc5741e74/libgcc/config/nds32/lib1asmsrc-mculib.S#L2099)\n-  Software floating-point multiply of Andes official version : 3 ~ 4 us.\n\nIT8320\u0027s floating-point division takes 32 cycles, so these two instructions will take total 64 cycles.\nPlus additional 24 instructions, __mulsf3 will take 1.83us (ideally, 1/48M*88).\nAs you mentioned, this patch has performance similar to floating-point library of official version if we pull code into ram. The difference is that this patch saves a little bit of code space.\n\nWe will also look into the URL to see if we are able to leverage the routine with N8 CPU’s instructions.",
      "parentUuid": "8b099ae1_f80a3d4c",
